Simple understanding

1. Built-in Algorithms
Use SageMaker's ready-made algorithms when you have a simple ML task and don't need custom code.

2. Script Mode ⭐
You write your own ML training code, while SageMaker provides the training environment/containers. This is useful when you have your own Python ML logic.

3. BYOC — Bring Your Own Container
You create/provide your own container, giving you maximum control over the environment.

4. Local Mode
Useful for development and testing before running larger training jobs.

5. Managed Spot Training
Useful for cost-sensitive jobs, using Spot capacity where applicable.

6. SageMaker Pipelines
Used for ML lifecycle automation—connecting steps such as processing, training, evaluation, and deployment.

7. Distributed Training
Used when training needs to scale across multiple compute resources, especially for large-scale deep learning.

8. Automatic Model Tuning
Used for hyperparameter tuning, where SageMaker searches for better hyperparameter combinations.

⭐ For your Insurance project

